# Cinematic mode's look (issue 20261030_142354: releasing RMB or switching the mode on flung the camera at ~200 deg/s).
# Run: python tools/harness/run.py tools/harness/scripts/cinematic_look.satcmd
# `inertial drag` holds the look button through the real look code (dx / dy px a frame, then a release whose cursor
# jump, warp_x / warp_y, arrives the frame after as GLFW's restore does); `state` -> camera.cinematic shows the rates.
#   1  switching cinematic mode on: no turn
#   2  a drag at 20 px/frame, released: coasts at the smoothed rate, capped (coast_deg_s <= 45), the warp ignored
#   3  holding the button with the mouse at rest stops the coast; a release at rest does not coast
time pause
set hud.right_panel.cinematic_mode true
wait 5
state
expect state.camera.cinematic.yaw_deg_s 0 tol=1e-6
inertial drag dx=20 frames=40 warp_x=-4000 warp_y=1500
wait 20
state
wait 25
state
wait 30
state
inertial drag dx=0 frames=40
wait 45
state
expect state.camera.cinematic.yaw_deg_s 0 tol=1e-6
set hud.right_panel.cinematic_mode false
wait 3
state
